==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/səbˈmæɹɪnə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/səbməˈɹiːnɚ/}} or {{IPA|/səbˈmɛɹɪnɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of the [[crew]] of a [[submarine]].
# {{context|US|baseball|lang=en}} A [[pitcher]] that throws with an underhand motion.
#: ''Jones was a '''submariner''' and could often confuse a batter with his unorthodox delivery.''

====Usage notes====
* This word is generally pronounced like ''[[sub-]]'' + ''[[mariner]]'' (for example, in the U.K. Royal Navy); however, since the prefix ''sub-'' can arguably imply inferiority (as in ''[[subpar]]'' or ''[[subhuman]]''), this pronunciation can be considered offensive by some, especially in the U.S. Navy. The pronunciation ''[[submarine]]'' + ''[[-er]]'', but with stress on third syllable, is therefore thought to be preferred by many or most U.S. submarine crew members today.

